  "reason": "The best-performing configuration so far is config_036 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) at 0.7150 acc. The only aggregation method tested in this top regime is avgpool. Prior evidence (config_018 vs 020) showed avgpool > transformer by ~4 pts, but that was in a much weaker regime (pca_n2000 + resnet50). With the substantially stronger scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l encoders, the feature representations are richer and a transformer aggregation might better capture cross-profile interactions, potentially closing or reversing the gap. Config_038 (transformer, concat) is the minimal, logical extension of the best config that tests whether the aggregation choice is a binding constraint in this regime. If it matches or beats avgpool, it opens a new design axis; if it underperforms, it confirms avgpool is optimal and frees budget to explore other dimensions. This is the highest-information single experiment because it directly probes the one untested variable in the current best configuration."
}

